# DB state after the fleet's hour: table links, 4 rows.
#
# Written by: Manager.pollTopology → topology.Builder.Build → queries.UpsertLink (MarkStaleLinksDown, DeleteOldLinks)
# The hour:   the call-plan fleet of 5 fake devices (callplan_harness_test.go), every scheduled loop,
#             one simulated hour and a minute from 2026-01-05 12:00 UTC; the devices' counters, CPU,
#             memory and uptime move with the clock (callplan_motion_test.go)
#
# A change in this file is a change in what the pollers store.
# Rewrite it with: go test ./internal/poller -run TestDBState -update
#
# Normalised (dbstate_test.go):
#   last_seen: SQLite's CURRENT_TIMESTAMP (wall clock) → <sqlite-now>; stored as TEXT "2006-01-02 15:04:05" (as CURRENT_TIMESTAMP writes it)
#   id: a generated id → <uuid-n>, numbered by first appearance
#   REAL values with three decimals, strings quoted, NULL as NULL
#   rows ordered by all their columns as shown

id=<uuid-1> device_a_id="ap-ac" interface_a="ether1" device_b_id="sw48" interface_b="ether2" link_type="ethernet" discovered_by="mndp" status="up" last_seen=<sqlite-now>
id=<uuid-2> device_a_id="ap-ax" interface_a="ether1" device_b_id="sw48" interface_b="ether1" link_type="ethernet" discovered_by="mndp" status="up" last_seen=<sqlite-now>
id=<uuid-3> device_a_id="rtr" interface_a="sfp-sfpplus1" device_b_id="sw48" interface_b="sfp-sfpplus1" link_type="ethernet" discovered_by="mndp" status="up" last_seen=<sqlite-now>
id=<uuid-4> device_a_id="sw24" interface_a="sfp-sfpplus1" device_b_id="sw48" interface_b="sfp-sfpplus2" link_type="ethernet" discovered_by="mndp" status="up" last_seen=<sqlite-now>
